a43f057182050fcde58767d4753cf414a9e5961fe0ac89c98e749ae4e","event_uuid":"202bbccf-365f-46c9-b506-7b0a3c44a701","position":{"commit_sha":"39bd814dc102a23a400ce813b8e0d23f5663a512","position":"1787045580936327001-202bbccf-365f-46c9-b506-7b0a3c44a701"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"bed7656702b4742cd5fbda8cebb47269da745de84bc795cc6204b24c255f112d","event_uuid":"d13e9ea4-b29b-44ca-afdf-8871cdfbacee","position":{"commit_sha":"8cfa572c12c580aae752fb2f9347fc28fd74e47d","position":"1787046576972496704-d13e9ea4-b29b-44ca-afdf-8871cdfbacee"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Confirmed Phase 1 RCA before repair.\n\nMechanism: `attach_commits` resolves ticket storage independently, but then passes that tracker path to `commit_impact.unresolvable_shas`; `code_root_for` defines the code repository as `dirname(tracker)`. With an absolute relocated store, valid code SHAs are therefore checked by `git -C <tracker-parent> rev-parse` instead of against the caller/current code checkout (`src/rebar/_lib_mutations.py:255,269`; `src/rebar/_engine_support/commit_impact.py:135-147`).\n\nRuntime proof in disposable separate code/store trees: the unchanged CLI command rejected valid `HEAD`; instrumentation captured `git -C /tmp/rebar-attach-rca-9918.Xt20YN/external rev-parse ... HEAD^{commit}`. Direct A/B validation returned `[]` at the code root and `[HEAD]` at the tracker parent. Even `rebar.attach_commits(..., repo_root=<code-root>)` still traced the tracker parent and failed, rejecting the CLI-omission rival. Monkeypatching only `code_root_for` to the code checkout made the valid attachment record a COMMITS event while a bogus SHA remained rejected, ruling out ticket lookup, append, Git, and all-or-nothing validation failures. A default in-repo tracker control continued to succeed.\n\nLegitimacy: defect. Relocated stores are explicitly supported (`src/rebar/_config_sources.py:64-67`, `docs/config.md:208-212`), while the attach contract requires each SHA to resolve in the repository (`src/rebar/_guides/commit-ticket-trailer.md:54-71`).\n\nCaller gate: only `_lib_mutations.attach_commits` calls the tracker-derived helpers. CLI, library, and MCP converge on this seam, and no caller depends on tracker-parent validation. Expected post-fix behavior: code SHA validation uses explicit `repo_root`, then `REBAR_ROOT`, then the cwd Git top-level, while tracker reads/writes continue through `REBAR_TRACKER_DIR`; genuinely unknown SHAs remain all-or-nothing failures.","timestamp":1787044279580268001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Final rebar-debug report (local repair complete; not pushed or closed).\n\nProblem: `attach_commits` rejected valid code commits when `REBAR_TRACKER_DIR` relocated ticket storage outside the code checkout.\n\nProven root cause: `_lib_mutations.attach_commits` passed the tracker path into `commit_impact.unresolvable_shas`; `code_root_for` then used `dirname(tracker)` as the code repository. Runtime tracing observed `git -C <tracker-parent> rev-parse`, so a valid code SHA was looked up in the wrong repository (`src/rebar/_lib_mutations.py:255,269`; former `src/rebar/_engine_support/commit_impact.py:135-147`).\n\nProof: the same real `HEAD` returned resolvable at the code root and unresolvable at the relocated tracker parent. Passing explicit `repo_root=<code-root>` still failed and traced the tracker parent, rejecting the CLI-omission rival. Changing only the validation root made the valid attachment persist while a bogus SHA remained rejected. Default nested tracker behavior succeeded.\n\nTest: `tests/interfaces/store/test_commits_on_ticket.py::test_attach_resolves_code_repo_independently_from_relocated_tracker` uses a real Git checkout and independently moved real tracker. It proves the dangerous preconditions, exact attachment receipt/persisted COMMITS state, and mixed valid/invalid all-or-nothing state. It was collected and observed RED before repair at the valid-commit call, GREEN after repair, then RED again under the exact `tracker.parent` mutation; restoration returned GREEN. The final-form raw-regex lint adjustment was also re-proven RED under the mutation before the fix was restored. The oracle asserts public return/persisted state, so behavior-preserving internal refactors do not break it.\n\nFix: validate the whole batch with `commit_impact.invalid_commit_shas(..., str(config.repo_root(repo_root)))`, preserving tracker lookup/append through `REBAR_TRACKER_DIR`. Delete `code_root_for` and `unresolvable_shas`, whose only production reference was this call chain, so the invalid tracker-derived prior art cannot be reused.\n\nScope and safety: CLI (`_commands/attach_commits.py:28`), MCP (`_mcp_writes.py:89-97`), and public library all converge on `_lib_mutations.attach_commits`; no caller depends on tracker-parent validation. This restores the documented relocated-store contract, adds no dependency or capability, preserves all-or-nothing state, and weakens no existing test. Repository search finds no remaining production `code_root_for` or `unresolvable_shas`.\n\nSiblings/parity: construct sweep covered the exact commit-validation helper/call family; no additional `invalid_commit_shas` caller derives code root from tracker storage. The previously confirmed close-precheck sibling was already repaired by parent `tekite-fleece-hake`/merged commit `548e4d2997`. Parity rule: attach-commits SHA validation must use the code repository independently of tracker storage. CLI, MCP, and library all hold through the shared seam; automated caller is N/A (none); the close-side consumer does not validate newly attached input and its analogous code-root defect is the merged parent fix. No parity slot is missing.\n\nVerification: focused attach/store selection 31 passed; full `tests/interfaces/store` reached 433 passed, 9 skipped, with one deterministic unrelated current-main failure in `test_bridge_preview_under_sync_contention_heldout` (`ModuleNotFoundError: rebar_reconciler`). `make lint` passed, `make typecheck` passed, and `git diff --check` passed. The unrelated failure reproduces alone and is filed as `fibrous-fabulous-dungbeetle` (79c6-eaf3-38af-4ce9), linked discovered_from this bug.\n\nResidual risk/prevention: the only observed residual is that pre-existing reconciler import failure; disposition: ticket filed as `fibrous-fabulous-dungbeetle`. No residual fragility observed in the attach-commits repair.\n\nReplication: the original disposable CLI scenario now prints `commits attached ...: 1` with the external tracker and persists exactly `commits: [{sha: HEAD}]`; a subsequent `HEAD definitely-not-a-commit` batch still errors `nothing was recorded` and leaves the single existing attachment unchanged.","timestamp":1787045535631540001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Local commit prepared for the serialized Gerrit queue: `d9cae80ca02c64f8f66d5ef14142452669247e38` (`Change-Id: Idcc306e35000e0a119ff15eac1d209b70c317648`). It carries the full `rebar-ticket: 9918-a5d6-8fb5-42e8` trailer and DCO sign-off; `rebar verify-commit-ticket --rev HEAD` resolves successfully. The worktree is clean. Per the one-global-CI-run rule, this change is intentionally not pushed or closed.","timestamp":1787045580936327001}],"created_at":1787025712617194001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"d13e9ea4-b29b-44ca-afdf-8871cdfbacee","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"39a9-d443-c539-46a7"}],"description":"## Context\nA deterministic relocated-store experiment confirmed that `src/rebar/_engine_support/commit_impact.py::code_root_for` conflates tracker storage with the code repository. `attach_commits` reaches it through `_lib_mutations.py`; with an absolute `REBAR_TRACKER_DIR` outside the code checkout, valid code commit SHAs are checked against the tracker parent and rejected. Runtime tracing observed `git -C <tracker-parent> rev-parse` while the same SHA resolved at the code root.\n\n## Plan\n- Add a real-git held-out regression oracle with a code repository and independently relocated ticket store.\n- Resolve commit validation from `config.repo_root(repo_root)` (explicit root, then `REBAR_ROOT`, then cwd Git top-level), while retaining tracker reads/writes through `REBAR_TRACKER_DIR`.\n- Remove the obsolete tracker-parent code-root helpers so the invalid derivation cannot remain as unused prior art.\n- Preserve all-or-nothing rejection for unknown SHAs and the default in-repo tracker path.\n- Run RED to GREEN, exact-defect mutation, focused store and attach suites, lint, typecheck, and original CLI replication.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] A valid code commit is accepted when the ticket store is outside the code worktree.\n- [x] An unknown SHA remains rejected without recording a partial COMMITS event.\n- [x] Default in-repo tracker behavior remains unchanged.\n- [x] The held-out relocated-store test is observed RED before repair and GREEN after repair.\n- [x] The exact tracker-parent mutation returns the held-out test to RED.\n- [x] `code_root_for` and `unresolvable_shas` have no remaining production definitions or references, checked by repository search.\n- [x] Focused tests pass.\n- [x] `make lint` passes.\n- [x] `make typecheck` passes.\n\n## Testing\n- `pytest tests/interfaces/store/test_commits_on_ticket.py tests/unit/test_attach_commits.py`\n- `grep -R \"code_root_for\\|unresolvable_shas\" src/rebar` must return no matches.\n- `make lint`\n- `make typecheck`","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_lib_mutations.py","reason":"resolve the code repository independently for attach-commits validation"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine_support/commit_impact.py","reason":"remove the obsolete tracker-parent code-root helper contract"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/store/test_commits_on_ticket.py","reason":"cover valid and invalid attachments with relocated tracker storage"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["parent","57b6-90b7-87bb-45e7"],["relates_to","39a9-d443-c539-46a7"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"57b6-90b7-87bb-45e7","parent_status_uuid":"1c5f772b-8c66-4600-9bf9-d05a1ab1354a","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["cli","git","tracker"],"ticket_id":"9918-a5d6-8fb5-42e8","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Resolve attach-commits code root independently from relocated tracker storage","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["97fbede5-a523-4d94-9db8-c5935ce71bd2","1c5f772b-8c66-4600-9bf9-d05a1ab1354a","bc530f5e-7613-4915-9e15-e4c2e2c5406c","c40489dd-9442-4486-9067-bdc54afd51cc","c0cf8815-952e-44ed-b840-bf5dc6132cb2","b0b2330a-dc88-4f71-ab59-35610ed2fb3b","e4c579b0-ae2d-4dca-a2c6-4624ac87a887","d466625d-fb4d-4395-b1d5-48e0d0022276","adc06ac5-ef2c-4214-9018-4109afb5fd15","ea07e14d-4fdf-4b93-8ec9-cad92eceeb0b","202bbccf-365f-46c9-b506-7b0a3c44a701","d13e9ea4-b29b-44ca-afdf-8871cdfbacee"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787046576972496705,"uuid":"05956069-6b3e-4608-8e2b-2444a64f86d8"}